.expect(check)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each check records a Swift Testing issue, at the caller’s source location, for every rule the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination breaks, and throws what the factory throws. Unlike a project’s own tests, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write their assertions out in full, this is a published assertion, shared on purpose, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TrackingPlanTesting’s "},{"code":"expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is: every vendor module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs the same checks. The checks send through the transport only, never the network, and run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in well under a second; give the calling suite a "},{"code":".timeLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as a factory that keeps a copy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the destination it returns makes a check wait for ever."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"DestinationTesting"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DestinationConformance","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DestinationConformance"}],"externalID":"s:18DestinationTesting0A11ConformanceV","title":"DestinationConformance","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance.swift#L41","fileName":"DestinationConformance.swift"}},"references":{"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/DestinationConformance/init(limit:timestamp:bodyText:makeRevealingDestination:makeDestination:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/destinationconformance\/init(limit:t